1. await will block current coroutine and jump to other coroutine, yield the control, when current coroutine is not blocking, jump back
2. do not use block function in async function, do not use block function like time.sleep, use non-blocking asyncio.sleep,
 do not await requests.post, do await non-blocking aiohttp.requests.post
3. only async function can call async function, use asyncio.get_running_loop get current loop, 

asyncio.get_running_loop then creat task will start task 
use asyncio.get_running_loop().create_task(async_func()) to call async_func in regular func,
if you don't need async func's return value in regular func, async_func won't block regular func
use loop.run_until_complete(future) will get async func return value in regular func and blocking regular func

use future = asyncio.get_running_loop().create_task(async_func()) in regular func
loop = asyncio.get_running_loop()
result = loop.run_until_complete(future) to get async function result in regular function
use result = await future to get async function result in async function

loop.run_until_complete(future) is blocking, not return control until future is complete, it just wait one future, automatically close the event loop
await asyncio.gather(future1,future2) wait for multiple futures
loop.run_forever() keeps the loop running continuously, until loop.stop()


use asyncio.get_running_loop after loop.run_forever() or asyncio.run()
use asyncio.get_event_loop before loop.run_forever() or asyncio.run()


async def f():
 loop = asyncio.get_running_loop()

async def main():
    loop = asyncio.get_event_loop()
    loop.create_task(f())

asyncio.run(main())


